---
/**
 * What is actually deployed, drawn from the two wrangler.jsonc files and the
 * two Worker entries rather than from a sketch.
 *
 * IT DISAGREES WITH 01 §2's ASCII DRAWING, DELIBERATELY. That diagram puts the
 * chat and analysis endpoints on the site Worker; they are on the MCP Worker,
 * because both need the `ai` binding and an `ai` binding cannot exist in the
 * config `astro build` instantiates (the CI failure is written up in both
 * wrangler.jsonc files). Publishing the spec's version on the page whose whole
 * premise is that its figures are checkable would be self-refuting -- the first
 * reader to `curl` the two endpoints would find the picture wrong. Verified
 * 2026-09-11 against ./wrangler.jsonc, workers/mcp/wrangler.jsonc,
 * src/worker.ts and workers/mcp/src/index.ts.
 *
 * NO UNLISTED ROUTE IS NAMED HERE, and that is the one thing this diagram
 * deliberately leaves out. src/worker.ts flattens every refusal on the
 * token-scoped prefix into the site's own 404 precisely so that a stranger
 * cannot tell a real route from a dead one; printing that path on a public page
 * would hand back the route-existence oracle the flattening exists to close.
 * "the form surfaces" is the honest aggregate, and it is all this page owes.
 *
 * INLINE SVG, NEVER AN `<img>`: the diagram has to follow the visitor's theme,
 * and an image cannot. Strokes are `currentColor` so the box work inherits the
 * ink token, the quieter lines take `--color-rule` through Tailwind's
 * `stroke-rule`, and there is no hex anywhere in this file.
 *
 * It is SCALED rather than scrolled -- `w-full` inside a `viewBox` -- so the
 * whole picture survives a 400px viewport. The cost is honest: the type inside
 * it shrinks with the drawing, which is why `max-w-md` caps how large it gets
 * on a wide screen (a diagram scaled to 1000px would have 32px labels) and why
 * the line count per box is kept low enough that 11.5 user units is legible at
 * the small end.
 *
 * `<title>` and `<desc>` with `aria-labelledby` are what a screen reader gets;
 * `role="img"` stops it from walking the 40-odd shapes underneath.
 */
---

<figure class="mt-10">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 400 542"
    class="h-auto w-full max-w-md"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="architecture-title architecture-desc"
    fill="none"
  >
    <title id="architecture-title">How this site is deployed</title>
    <desc id="architecture-desc">
      Two Cloudflare Workers. Visitors and agents reach the site Worker at ryanlindsey.me, which
      serves the pages, the résumé in four formats, llms.txt, the markdown variants and the feeds,
      hosts the chat page and the form surfaces, and runs the queue consumer that sends the
      notification email. It calls the MCP Worker at mcp.ryanlindsey.me over a service binding for
      the MCP endpoint, for chat and for form posts; the MCP Worker calls back the same way to read
      published documents. The MCP Worker holds the MCP endpoint as a Durable Object, the streamed
      chat inference, the discovery routes, the AI Gateway path to Anthropic and the Workers AI path
      to Vectorize. Both Workers share D1 for the audit log, tokens, transcripts and eval runs, KV
      for caches and flags, R2 for generated PDFs and documents, and Analytics Engine feeding the
      events queue.
    </desc>

    {/* Visitors and agents */}
    <rect x="90" y="4" width="220" height="34" class="fill-surface" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
    <text x="200" y="26" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" class="font-mono fill-current"
      >Visitors and agents</text
    >

    {/* ... down to the site Worker */}
    <path d="M200,38 L200,64" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M196,58 L200,64 L204,58" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <text x="208" y="55" font-size="10" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted">HTTPS</text>

    {/* The site Worker */}
    <rect x="20" y="64" width="360" height="134" class="fill-surface" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
    <text x="32" y="86" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-current"
      >Site Worker &#183; ryanlindsey.me</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="108" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >Astro SSR over the static assets</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="124" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >pages, posts, case studies, r&#233;sum&#233;</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="140" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >/llms.txt, .md variants, RSS and JSON</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="156" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >/chat page and the form surfaces</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="172" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >the queue consumer that sends the email</text
    >

    {/* The binding cycle: site to MCP, and MCP back to the site */}
    <path d="M120,198 L120,250" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M116,244 L120,250 L124,244" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <text x="128" y="214" font-size="10" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted">/mcp, chat and forms</text
    >
    <path d="M280,250 L280,198" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M276,204 L280,198 L284,204" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <text x="272" y="240" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >document reads</text
    >

    {/* The MCP Worker */}
    <rect x="20" y="250" width="360" height="134" class="fill-surface" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
    <text x="32" y="272" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-current"
      >MCP Worker &#183; mcp.ryanlindsey.me</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="294" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >/mcp endpoint, a Durable Object</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="310" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >POST /chat, the streamed inference</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="326" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >/robots.txt, /.well-known/mcp.json</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="342" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >AI Gateway &#8594; Anthropic</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="358" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >Workers AI &#8594; Vectorize, for retrieval</text
    >

    {/* ... down to what both of them share */}
    <path d="M200,384 L200,416" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M196,410 L200,416 L204,410" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <text x="208" y="404" font-size="10" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted">bindings</text>

    {/* The shared stores, bussed to both Workers down the left margin */}
    <path
      d="M6,131 L6,474 M6,131 L20,131 M6,317 L20,317 M6,474 L20,474"
      class="stroke-rule"
      stroke-dasharray="3 4"></path>
    <rect x="20" y="416" width="360" height="116" class="fill-surface" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
    <text x="32" y="438" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-current">Shared by both Workers</text>
    <text x="32" y="460" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >D1 &#183; audit, tokens, transcripts, evals</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="476" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >KV &#183; caches and flags</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="492" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >R2 &#183; generated PDFs and documents</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="508" font-size="11.5" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >Analytics Engine &#8594; the events queue</text
    >
  </svg>

  <figcaption class="mt-4 max-w-prose font-mono text-micro text-ink-muted">
    Drawn from the deployed configuration &mdash; the two <code>wrangler.jsonc</code> files and the two
    Worker entries in{' '}
    <a class="text-accent underline" href="https://github.com/ryanlindsey/ryanlindsey.me"
      >the repository</a
    > &mdash; rather than from a sketch, so it can be checked against what is running.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
